<ix:footnote id="ix_41_footnote" xml:lang="en-US">The impact on the fair value measurement of an increase in each unobservable input is in isolation. The discount rate is the rate used to discount future cash flows in a discounted cash flow calculation. An increase in the discount rate, in isolation, would result in a decrease in the fair value measurement. Market Multiples refer to the input (often derived from the value of a comparable company) that is multiplied by the historic and/or expected EBITDA of a company in order to estimate the company&#8217;s value. An increase in the Market Multiples, in isolation, would result in an increase in the fair value measurement.</ix:footnote><!--Text not found in footnote sections assigned to Schedule of Quantitative Information about Level 3 Fair Value Measurements-->
